// max10-x.lmc - input 10 numbers into a row, then find the largest (extended LMC, NOT part of OCR's LMC)
// Compare with ../max10.lmc, which never stores the numbers. Keeping them in a row (INDEXED addressing)
// means the program could look at them again, for example to find the smallest as well.
// Input: 3 9 2 7 10 1 8 4 6 5      Output: 10
        LDX #0
read    INP
        STA data,X      // data[X] = the number just typed
        INX
        TXA
        SUB #10         // have 10 numbers been read?
        BRZ scan
        BRA read
scan    LDA data        // the first number is the largest so far
        STA max
        LDX #1          // start looking at the second number
look    LDA data,X
        SUB max         // data[X] - max
        BRP bigger      // 0 or more: data[X] is at least as big as max
after   INX
        TXA
        SUB #10
        BRZ done        // looked at all 10
        BRA look
bigger  LDA data,X
        STA max         // remember the new largest
        BRA after
done    LDA max
        OUT
        HLT
max     DAT
data    DAT             // the row is the empty mailboxes from here on
